# matugen template — wallpaper-adaptive fuzzel colours.
#
# Rendered by set-wallpapers (via ~/.config/matugen/config.toml [templates.fuzzel]) to
# ~/.cache/quickshell/fuzzel-colors on every wallpaper change. The ~/.config/hypr/scripts/fz
# launcher reads this file and passes each line as a fuzzel flag, so fuzzel recolours to the
# wallpaper (and flips light/dark with it) exactly like the Quickshell shell — instead of the
# static purple hardcoded in fuzzel.ini (which stays only as the fallback if this file is
# missing). hex_stripped gives RRGGBB; the trailing 2 hex digits are the alpha fuzzel wants.
# NOTE: --background-color is NOT here — set-wallpapers appends it after matugen runs, using
# the `source` dominant darkened by the same 0.80 factor as the shell's popupBg, so fuzzel's
# panel matches the other popups. (matugen has no relative-darken filter.)
--text-color={{colors.on_surface.default.hex_stripped}}ff
--prompt-color={{colors.primary.default.hex_stripped}}ff
--input-color={{colors.on_surface.default.hex_stripped}}ff
--placeholder-color={{colors.on_surface_variant.default.hex_stripped}}aa
--match-color={{colors.primary.default.hex_stripped}}ff
--selection-color={{colors.secondary_container.default.hex_stripped}}ff
--selection-text-color={{colors.on_secondary_container.default.hex_stripped}}ff
--selection-match-color={{colors.primary.default.hex_stripped}}ff
--border-color={{colors.outline.default.hex_stripped}}cc
--counter-color={{colors.on_surface_variant.default.hex_stripped}}aa
